WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.410
<i>On days when something good happened,</i>

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.350
On days when

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.350
something good happened,

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:05.910
<i>I always liked to go
to bed without a bath.</i>

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:07.690
I

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.690
always liked to go to bed

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.690
without a bath.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.040
Haruka, take your bath!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:12.890
No!

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.760
Then get in with your daddy!

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.010
That's even worse...

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.810
<i>I felt like I could still smell the good</i>

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.040
<i>memory of that day on my body,</i>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.470
<i>and that the water
would wash it all off.</i>

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:32.670
Wow, Mont Saint-Michel is
beautiful even from a distance.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.400
Is it?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.810
I just want to get in the bath

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.680
and wash off this sticky sea air.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.810
<i>When I think about it now,</i>

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.050
<i>I guess I'm still a child.</i>

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.190
Nu...

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.190
Nuits-St.-Georges.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.700
Looks like we're finally in Burgundy.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.960
We get off next, at Beaune Station.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.860
Hasegawa-san might come to Beaune.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.700
Yeah.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.280
It's kind of weird seeing
Nuits-St.-Georges and Beaune

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.870
as actual places,
and not just labels on wine bottles.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.340
I don't know much about wine,
so it's all over my head.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.300
Wine is the nation's culture.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.090
No matter how much you
know about France,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.810
if you don't know wine,
it's not even worth considering.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.190
There's nothing to worry about, though.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.670
Yeah, wine is just another
alcoholic beverage.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.810
So, Sawaki...

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.720
Have you picked up any
Hasegawa microbes yet?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.700
Not a trace, as of right now.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.460
But if this is really the
entrance to Burgundy,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.090
Hasegawa-san is sure to pass through.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.200
Paris - Gare de Lyon

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.200
Dijon Bourgogne Airport

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.200
Beaune

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.960
Dijon Airport

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.620
We can go straight to
Beaune by car from here.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.210
It's the boonies,
but it's a really nice place.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.570
Burgundy...

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.850
You do know I'm not
going to drink, right?

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.360
I guess we just wait at the station.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.610
Either that,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.420
or we look for churches that

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.520
might be hosting the wedding.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.620
Just a thought,

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.210
but is Hasegawa really the kind of girl

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.970
who would come straight here?

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.950
Huh?

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.780
But this is her wedding, right?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.030
She wouldn't bail on that... would she?

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.340
I can see it.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.040
Yes.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:36.510
Moyashimon

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.510
Returns

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.470
Mud puddle!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.450
Go around, go around!

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.100
This region is Côte-d'Or.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.020
Does it have any churches?

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.670
All I see are fields.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.230
I guess grapes aren't really
grown by stringing them up.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.090
Wine grapes are planted densely,

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.670
so they're always hungry as they grow.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:26.760
When they're planted close together,

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.490
the roots have to grow long and deep.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.740
The idea is that, if the vines
are free to grow at leisure,

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.860
they can send all their nutrients
to the grape bunches.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.400
Each vine produces about eight bunches.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.510
That's about a third
of a bottle of wine.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.420
So even with grapes as
far as the eye can see,

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.100
it still doesn't yield that much wine.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.640
Look, it's the Romanée-Conti vineyard.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.780
They're so small...

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.300
They're growing right next
to so many other vines.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.650
What makes Romanée-Conti so different?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.750
Something is different.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.150
I just don't know what.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.170
If this is Romanée-Conti, that means

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.530
we've reached the Route des Grand Crus.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.120
Hey!

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.500
That looks promising.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.670
It sure does.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.710
We actually got here pretty easily, huh?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.110
Watch out! Mud puddle!

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.580
We're wobbling!

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.590
Car!

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.620
Everyone okay?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.300
Yeah...

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.020
Yes.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.210
Damn it! Are you okay?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.110
Relax, Marie!

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.110
Who are these people?

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.610
Why did they crash into my car?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.350
She looks like Kei!

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.640
Who is that?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.600
Oops, looks like we're on.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:06:08.630
Wine is...

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.620
Well, Tadayasu and his friends'
adventures with running

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.950
into girls who look like Kei
and such will continue shortly.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.310
But now A. oryzae and...

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.530
S. cerevisiae will give
you a simple explanation

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.630
of some complicated facts about wine.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.110
Wine is an alcoholic beverage
made by fermenting grapes.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.680
The naturally occurring beverage has
a long history alongside mankind.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.640
Even the ancient Greeks
drank lots of it.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:28.650
Wine Producing Regions of the World

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:28.650
50° North

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.510
Now, along with beer,

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.850
it is produced all around the globe,

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:23.970
representing a whole world of liquors.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:26.570
The number one wine

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.650
in many respects is French wine.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.890
Champagne
Alsace

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.890
Belgium

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.890
Mediterranean Sea

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.960
Today we'll tell you all about the wine

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.010
produced in Burgundy,

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.910
where Tadayasu and his friends are.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.040
Yonne

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.580
Côte-d'Or

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.190
Burgundy is a vineyard region that
stretches nearly 300 kilometers

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:40.390
from Chablis in the north
to Beaujolais in the south.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:42.750
Saône-et-Loire

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:43.420
Grapes used to make Burgundy
wine are cultivated here.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.420
Rhone

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:48.890
Loosely speaking,
Burgundy wine is classified by region.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:51.450
The highest classification, Grand Cru,

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.100
refers to the highest grade vineyards.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.900
Just because wine is
high grade and expensive

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.040
doesn't mean it'll taste great.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.440
The final product differs
depending on the maker.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.200
A skilled maker can produce

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.790
wine with better flavor than
the highest grade wines,

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.440
and the reverse is possible, too.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:16.950
Wine is...

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.580
Anyway, Tadayasu and his friends

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.740
have just met a French
girl who looks like Kei.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.600
What will happen next?

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.790
Will they find Haruka?

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.950
Okay, see you later!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:23.800
I asked, and they said
there's no wedding here.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.960
Besides, this isn't a church.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.850
It's not a church?

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.970
So much for running off with the bride.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.080
Who are you guys?

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:35.970
You're not dressed like people
who are going to a wedding.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.720
We're not here to cause any trouble.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.330
We came here from Japan
to look for our friend.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.730
And that friend is the bride-to-be?

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:47.980
Yes. You could say it's sort of
a political marriage crisis.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:51.790
Truth is, if we don't find her,
we'll be in a lurch, too.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:52.750
Huh?

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.110
Anyway,

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.380
the only thing we know for sure
is that the wedding is taking place

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.400
somewhere in the middle of
the Route des Grand Crus.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.500
Well, it's got nothing to do with me,

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.540
but this place is called the
Château du Clos de Vougeot,

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.250
and it used to be a monastery.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.480
So it must be at some other church.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.600
Was Mutou-san's information even right?

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.010
We're seriously in for it
if we don't find Hasegawa!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.220
Well, I'll be going now.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:19.880
What?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.000
I mean, you're all okay, right?

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.110
And I even translated for you!

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:29.920
Ow! It hurts!

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.890
No! That's low!

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.990
You Japanese people play dirty!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.380
A Burgundy girl who
can speak Japanese...

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:40.610
I guess luck really was on our side.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.070
We'd better not let
her out of our sight.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.000
Yeah.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.940
I can hear you.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.360
Ah, Marie...

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:50.380
you should have hit these
guys harder in that crash.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.590
No money, no place to stay,

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.030
and now they're even
pretending to be hurt.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.390
What do you mean, "pretending"?
That's rude!

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.020
I understand that you want
to find your friend,

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.910
but if you want to stay at my place,

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.650
you're going to have to do some work.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.150
We're going to make you apologize

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.930
to the bike rental shop, you know.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.590
Leave it to a returnee from overseas!

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:12.630
You won't even cave in
to a Burgundy girl, huh?

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:13.860
Leave it to me!

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.410
There's a small banquet
happening at my home today.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.900
If you'll work as waiters,
I'll give you some beds.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.660
We have experience as garçons.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.900
No matter who the guests are,
just leave them to us.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.750
It's just a pointless banquet,

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.790
so even weird-looking outsiders,
like you guys, won't stand out.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.600
Wow, what a mansion...

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.350
Domaines in France really are like castles...

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.350
Domaine = A privately owned vineyard where wine is brewed and bottled.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.770
Is that you, Marie? How you've grown!

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.720
Thanks for your help.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.850
I forgot...

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.280
I was irritated with them.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.050
By the way, Marie and these gentlemen

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.850
are speaking in French.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:58.110
Bonjour!

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.900
Did the winery have it ready for you?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.410
If you wanted arrangements for
wine produced somewhere else,

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.120
you might as well have had
this banquet in a restaurant.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.700
Sorry, Marie.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.430
It seems our guest today has just

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.830
recently taken interest in wine.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.190
Burgundy natives are supposed
to make fun of people

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.030
who think they're all into wine

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.040
by lying out our asses to them!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.480
I like that strategy,

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.580
but he's a work acquaintance
since my father's time,

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.140
so I just couldn't do that.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.430
But in exchange,

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:30.250
I intend to buy plenty
of wine from your father

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.770
and, of course, your grandfather.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:34.650
Besides, Marie...

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:37.840
Your grandfather plans to
retire this year, yes?

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.030
Will you at last make
your debut in the winery business?

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:43.780
Why should I?

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:49.020
Well, you were born into a
historical Burgundy domaine...

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.170
I won't do it.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.690
I'm only next in line because my brother

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:55.190
decided to run off and get
a job in Paris, right?

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:58.260
I can't accept such a
one-sided proposition.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.900
I have no idea what they're saying.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:02.210
She's mad.

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:03.600
Was it a bad idea for us to come?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.680
Let's bust a move!

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.670
Bring that wooden box from the back.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:07.920
Hey, Japanese.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:08.680
Bust a move?

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.340
Marie, who are those young men?

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.190
I just picked them up.
They're our garçons.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.560
When someone talks about
a banquet at a domaine,

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.010
they mean a wine drinking party.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.690
We don't serve a full
course or anything.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:22.700
You'll just hustle out about
three dishes, and that's it.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.450
It sounded like you were arguing earlier.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.820
Is everything okay?

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:28.150
Do you make wine, too?

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:30.960
He's actually the successor to
a long-standing business, too.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.580
His brother ran off,
so as the second son,

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.830
he was next in line to take over.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:37.960
Yeah, well...

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:41.720
I'm going to get out of this
dumb place and aim higher.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:45.150
I'll study as much as it takes to do it.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.220
I'll learn lots of other languages
besides Japanese, too.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.870
A Burgundy winery is a dumb place?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.980
I guess that's how it seems
to someone who was born here.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.250
Are you boys Japanese?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.870
Speaking French

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.950
Who's this guy?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.530
He's the chef in charge
of the meat tonight.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:10.870
Well, anyway, bonjour.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.620
Speaking French

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.500
That's perfect.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.500
The appetizer tonight is Japanese sashimi.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:15.750
Why?

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.580
Sashimi with wine?

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.430
It was the guest's request.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.590
I thought we'd be serving
the usual Burgundy cuisine,

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:23.760
so it threw me for a loop, too.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.420
Calling on a chef to make sashimi?!

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:27.690
You coordinate with the wine!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.280
What does he think he's playing at?

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:30.820
Is something wrong?

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.520
Are we fired already?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.270
They're talking about the food.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:37.270
The next course is beef,
so I'll make it count!

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:38.670
For God's sake!

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:41.250
If I don't say something,
I think I might go crazy!

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.870
If we get fired,

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:45.280
we'll be looking for
Hasegawa-san on foot.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.030
So, through the union of food and wine,

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.520
which I express as marriage,

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.780
or with respect to France, mariage...

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.830
I've been searching for a white
wine that matches sashimi,

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.040
Japan's very culture.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.240
You guys are here?

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.670
L-Long time no see.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.820
And to take it a step further,

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.680
This has nothing to do with us.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.390
as a mariage with Japanese sashimi.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.390
Just let him talk.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:10.080
This is something I
heard secondhand from a

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.390
Japanese friend of mine living in France.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.890
He said that France's
famous Guérande salt

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:19.520
is even better with sashimi
than wasabi and soy sauce.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:20.470
Huh?

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:21.330
Salt?

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.660
And that is another mariage...

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.440
Show some respect!

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.030
How could you put salt on sashimi?!

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:30.460
Your friend is just an idiotic Francophile!

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.580
W-What did you say?!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.700
Go, Sawaki!

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:34.580
Right!

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.210
A. oryzae to the rescue!

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:39.020
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:40.840
Now I remember!

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:43.520
You're the two guys who were in
the restaurant the other day!

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.050
What are you doing here?!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.410
This is the Japanese way.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.090
Merci.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.070
If you're going to have
sashimi with soy sauce,

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:52.600
you might as well drink sake,
not white wine.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:54.150
What are you saying?!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.790
Exchange this for a fresh
plate of sashimi, now!

00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:58.600
Are you...

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.500
the type who tries to
sound informed by saying

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.050
white wine goes with oysters?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.640
Wh-What?

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.740
What was all that about mariage?

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:08.580
If a Frenchman told you,

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:12.760
"I found the perfect orange juice
to pair with freshly cooked rice,"

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.240
would it make you happy?

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:15.980
Let me tell you something.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:18.750
Drinking beer to match the oil
used in Chinese food is fine,

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.170
but laojiu is a far better match.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.400
And beer works fine
with Korean barbecue,

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:25.160
but makgeolli is even better.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.050
You've gotta have tequila with tacos.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.730
If you want to drink wine
with sushi and tempura,

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.340
that's your choice,

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:33.670
but trying to match wine
with everything...

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:36.240
To me, it looks like you're
just playing around.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:37.560
Are you stupid?!

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.060
Am I not the host of this banquet?!

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:43.650
What's wrong with placing an
order that I'm paying for?!

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:46.500
This is what it's like, Grandpa.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.650
I'm not taking over this vineyard.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.660
What do we leave behind in
this world by making wine?

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.450
Is something that ends up stacked
in some rich guy's wine cellar,

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.160
only to disappear one day,
our pride and joy?

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.170
The Pinot and Chardonnay you
make are exquisite, Grandpa.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:06.580
Is even the main drink served
at the end of this banquet

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.670
going to be some foreign
alcohol that he chose?

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.840
This is a domaine!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.760
If it's just a hobby to you,
then do it somewhere else!

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:20.600
My deepest apologies, everyone.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.690
I will have fresh plates
served right away.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.190
Marie cannot take over the vineyard.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:29.190
It's unspeakable to think of a wine
maker choosing who drinks the wine.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.020
What the hell was all that about?

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:33.890
And in front of Haruka-san...
what an insult!

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:34.900
Are you that stupid?

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.200
You should feel humiliated.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.460
Sawaki, would you pull out my chair?

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.280
I'm leaving.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:45.440
Please forgive his... no, our rudeness.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.340
Should we really stay here tonight?

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:56.950
That's what worries you?
What about the money?!

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:58.810
Since Hasegawa left,

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.090
there's no need for us to stay here.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.230
Haruka!

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:04.870
How dare you belittle me?!

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.260
Who do you think I'm
doing all this for?!

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:13.850
At any rate, I've fulfilled
my obligation to Hasegawa.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:15.550
He can't say anything.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:17.410
But what will we do?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.340
With Marie behaving like that as her
grandfather's about to retire,

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.370
is this the end of the domaine?

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:26.360
Yes, and her father's wine
is second-rate at best.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.710
Looks like this is the
time for our company

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.800
to cut ties with this domaine.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:37.390
Miss Haruka has not yet
left the building...

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.190
I don't care!

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.490
There he goes.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.960
The driver will be back.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.400
I'm going to look for Marie.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.760
Please find her, Sawaki.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.910
I need to apologize to her.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:59.270
I acted selfishly after accepting
an invitation to her château.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.910
She has the right to be angry.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:02.620
But that aside,

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.790
what are you guys doing here?

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.920
Tell her, Kawahama.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:11.620
The professor sent us here
to buy wine and cheese.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.360
Yep.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:15.730
But we went through hell in Paris,
and now we're broke.

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:16.890
It's sad, really.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.300
So lend us some money, Hasegawa-san.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.270
You find me, and that's all you ask?

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.930
It's different for Sawaki, though.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.170
Sawaki came here on behalf of

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.940
everyone else to bring you back.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.820
What? Me?

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.920
I'm just here on vacation!

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.820
Even if no one came for me,
I'd go back home!

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.450
You're here to get married, aren't you?

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:42.510
Itsuki heard it straight from your dad.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:45.970
But the others don't think
that's what you really want.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.370
Wait a minute!

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.960
I haven't heard anything about this!

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.460
That was probably his intention.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.500
He can't say he didn't know,

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.470
after coming all the way out here.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.810
But no matter where I go or what I do,

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:02.220
in the end, I'm just a bird in a cage.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.520
Are you okay with that?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.310
Yeah. It's not like you.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.590
Ma—

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:11.320
What did he mean, he's the one paying?!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.380
There's no way that creep knows

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.940
the difference between wines!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.950
Don't you agree?!

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.500
I don't want to take
over the domaine

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.450
just to have jerks like
him kissing up to me!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:25.330
Ha-Hasegawa-san says she
wants to apologize to you.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.830
Not interested. I'm going to sleep.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.330
Tell her I was in bed naked.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:34.590
You guys can just find beds
wherever and get some rest.

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:43.640
<i>You should stir things
up now and then, too.</i>

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.770
Y-You didn't mean now,
did you, Aya-san?

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.360
I guess not.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.250
There he is.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.700
Sawaki, was Marie in?

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.600
She said she was going to sleep.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.570
She was naked.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:02.340
For real?!

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:03.700
We'll ask for details later.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.350
I see.

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:07.200
It's a shame, but I guess
I'll leave for now.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.480
Let's meet at the morning
market in Beaune tomorrow.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:12.210
I don't have my wallet, either.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:16.040
Give my regards to everyone here,
and to the girl, too.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.480
Ignoring her own will,
even when it's about her wedding...

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.270
She is?

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:28.430
I wonder how she feels as she's
going back to the hotel.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:32.320
If I were in her shoes,
I'd be feeling terrible.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:33.210
Yeah.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.730
I guess girls have it pretty rough, too.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.260
Are you taking an interest
in Marie now, Sawaki?

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:39.830
How did she look naked?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.400
What are you asking that for?

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:45.700
Well... her situation seems
really similar to mine.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:50.070
But I guess what makes
me and Marie different

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:55.500
is that I've never tried to find
an alternative to get out of it...

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:59.820
I've gotten word that
Ryuuta-san is in the

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:00.970
hotel lobby, drinking.

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.180
I see.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.190
Marriage?

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:08.970
He's only doing this for himself.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 8

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:56.950
We're S. cerevisiae!

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:59.590
We ferment sugar into alcohol!

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:02.920
Of course, we ferment wine, too!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.130
Hey-o!

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:07.310
There are lots of different wines.
Which kind is the tastiest?

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:08.970
Well...

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:12.140
Of all the different wines
fermented around the world,

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.480
the best wine comes from here!

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:16.890
Bordeaux

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:17.850
Burgundy

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:17.460
And of all the French wines, the big two

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:19.080
are Bordeaux and Burgundy.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:21.110
The bottles are different shapes.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:24.300
Burgundy

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:24.400
Bordeaux

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:22.280
That's right!

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:23.480
No matter where in the

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:24.960
world a wine comes from,

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.430
you can tell what type it is

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:28.020
by the shape of the bottle.

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:29.950
So, which kind is the tastiest?

00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:34.410
We can't explain everything in
such a short amount of time!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:35.750
What?!

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:39.880
Then, how can humans find good wine?

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:44.710
The best bet is to try all
different kinds and compare.

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:46.970
Yeah!

00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:48.300
Cheers!

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:49.970
Only
drink
alcohol
after
you
are
of
legal
age.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:50.390
Just don't drink too much!
